  "_note": "Arm rigs (docs/arm-rig-plan.md), keyed by art file. All points are fractions of the art square (0,0 top-left, 1,1 bottom-right). Per arm, named by the side of the IMAGE it is on (L = x < 0.5), not the character's own left: `upper` (the whole shoulder from the collar down to the elbow row, never past it: only its round elbow cap crosses the joint, or a bent elbow carries a chunk of forearm with it; owner 2026-11-12: the shoulder must move with the arm) and `fore` (from above the elbow to the fingertips) are the pieces' outlines (the forearm reaches up past the elbow, under the upper arm, which is drawn over it); `shoulder`, `elbow`, `grip` the joints; `cap` the radius (of the square's width) of the round disc both pieces carry at the elbow so a bend keeps the arm's full width (`shoulderCap`, a radius, adds one at the shoulder to the upper arm); `under` the part of the body the upper arm hides, painted in from the body's side (toward the image's centre) once the arm is cut away; `fill` how: smeared from the nearest solid pixel (default, plain cloth) or `clone`, a copy of the body `cloneStep` away ([du, dv], default a little further in; the Bear copies the flank from below), so fur keeps its texture; `blend` the half-widths of the shoulder and elbow weight ramps; `bulge` how much wider (1 = twice) the upper arm swells near the shoulder when the arm is level, fading out `bulgeReach` down the arm. Measured by hand on gridded crops 2026-11-12.",
